<title>UK: British election diary - March 26.</title>
<headline>British election diary - March 26.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the main election campaign-related events scheduled for Wednesday March 26.</p>
<p>- Prime Minister John Major tours northern England (no further details available)</p>
<p>- News conference by Conservative Party Chairman Brian Mawhinney, President of the Board of Trade Ian Lang and Economic Secretary to the Treasury Angela Knight at 0930 GMT.</p>
<p>- Conservative MP John Redwood holds book signing for his Our Country, Our Currency which opposes British membership of the single European currency, 1030 gmt, Books Etc, Victoria Street, London.</p>
<p>Labour Economics spokesman Gordon Brown visits Basildon.</p>
<p>15:35 media interviews ITEC</p>
<p>18:00 speech at Forte Posthouse Hotel.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7768</p>
